Going forward, please use this as the standard test recipe for every new model-route combination you evaluate: run basic inference, a forced tool call, a stateless tool result continuation, a cache-warm request, and then an identical replay of that same request to confirm the cache is actually read back rather than just written. Report raw numbers for each, not just pass or fail — token counts, the cache creation versus cache read breakdown, and whichever of success or model-not-found actually came back. If a model returns model-not-found, note that explicitly as provisioning-in-progress rather than a final result, and re-test once access should have propagated, since we've had cases where access wasn't available yet at first attempt. This applies to every future model and route you test, not just the two we just resolved.
